#
# The field controller's direct Python dependencies. requirements.txt is made
# from this file with every package pinned to a version and its PyPI hashes
# (every wheel and source archive of that version, so the same file installs
# on a Pi's aarch64, on x86-64, on Python 3.11 to 3.14). Only releases at least
# two weeks old are taken (--exclude-newer). To refresh both files, from the
# repository root:
#   docker run --rm -v "$PWD/controller:/w" -w /w python:3.12.14-slim sh -c '
#     pip install -q uv==0.9.30 &&
#     uv pip compile --universal --python-version 3.11 --exclude-newer YYYY-MM-DD \
#       --generate-hashes --no-header requirements.in -o requirements.txt'
# then put the SPDX header and the install notes back at the top of
# requirements.txt, and check that it still installs for the Pi (the commands
# are in controller/README.md, "Installing with pip").
